      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-15552",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following could be the graph of a continuous function $f(x)$ that satisfies the conditions below?\n\n- $f^{\u2032}(-2) = f^{\u2032}(2) = f^{\u2033}(0) = 0$\n- if $x \u2208 (- \u221e,-2)\u222a(2, \u221e)$ then $f^{\u2032}(x) > 0$ and if $x \u2208 (-2, 2)$ then $f^{\u2032}(x) < 0$\n- if $x \u2208 (- \u221e, 0)$ then $f^{\u2033}(x) < 0$ and if $x \u2208 (0, \u221e)$ then $f^{\u2033}(x) > 0$"
